1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
Good morning and welcome, everybody.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:07,800
I'm Jenny Stewart and I'm the Staff Manager here at the exhibition centre.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:13,605
We're expecting this year's International Travel Exhibition to attract over 10,000 visitors a day,

4
00:00:13,605 --> 00:00:20,570
ladies and gentlemen, and you are among the two hundred extra staff recruited to help look after them.

5
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:22,881
Now, to help things run smoothly,

6
00:00:22,881 --> 00:00:27,500
we have divided you into four teams. The blue team

7
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,200
the green team, the red team, and the yellow team.

8
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,208
So first I'll explain how the teams are divided up,

9
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:40,220
and then we'll be giving you colour-coded T-shirts so we can identify you more easily.

10
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:44,020
First of all, those who will be looking after the phones

11
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,786
and handling all calls regarding the exhibition,

12
00:00:46,786 --> 00:00:49,340
you will be on the red team.

13
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,502
Now, we've also put the entrance staff on the red team

14
00:00:53,502 --> 00:00:58,420
and you'll be stamping the entrance tickets and giving out publicity leaflets, OK?

15
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:03,090
Those of you involved in distributing entrance tickets will be on the yellow team

16
00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:05,425
and we've also put those of you

17
00:01:05,425 --> 00:01:10,095
who'll be staffing the information booths around the conference centre on the yellow team,

18
00:01:10,095 --> 00:01:12,430
so you'll be getting a yellow T-shirt.

19
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:17,820
Now, most of the hospitality staff have been put in the blue team

20
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:18,991
so the chefs among you

21
00:01:18,991 --> 00:01:23,060
and the kitchen hands will all need a blue T-shirt, but

22
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:24,823
because of the sheer numbers,

23
00:01:24,823 --> 00:01:28,580
all waiting staff will be on the yellow team

24
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:31,020
and this includes the bar staff among you.

25
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,340
Those who will be monitoring

26
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:37,285
and directing the traffic in the car parks are on the green team,

27
00:01:37,285 --> 00:01:40,070
so you'll need to get a green T-shirt.

28
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:48,000
This year we've also employed a considerable number of attendants to direct the human traffic around the conference centre.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,455
Now, you'll be working in the exhibition hall at all times,

30
00:01:52,455 --> 00:01:56,100
giving directions and generally helping people whenever you can,

31
00:01:56,100 --> 00:02:01,770
and you will be in the red team, so please collect a red T-shirt.

32
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:05,824
Right, now that everyone knows what team they're in, we'll get on

33
00:02:05,824 --> 00:02:11,230
with the orientation and training programmer and first I'll run through the rest of today's programme,

34
00:02:11,230 --> 00:02:15,500
which you should have in front of you

35
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,000
so that you can get a general idea of what else is in store today.

36
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,970
This introduction finishes at 9.30 and then you'll be hearing from Anne Smith.

37
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:32,540
Anne works in the accounts department on level two and she looks after all temporary staff,

38
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:38,700
and so she is the person to see if you have any problems regarding pay.

39
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,740
Anne will be explaining when and how you get this.

40
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,080
She will also be handing out your tax forms.

41
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:51,475
And I will just stress that all tax forms must be completed

42
00:02:51,475 --> 00:02:55,970
and returned to Anne before your pay can be processed.

43
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:00,205
Following Anne's talk you'll hear from Peter Chen, our Conference Manager,

44
00:03:00,205 --> 00:03:06,060
and he will be going over a plan of the conference centre with you

45
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,290
which will help you to orient yourselves.

46
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:12,620
He will also go through the security arrangements with you

47
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,960
and show you the fire exits.

48
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:20,700
Then at 10.30, there will be a coffee break in the staff canteen

49
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,310
which is located down on the ground floor.

50
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:30,418
Now, after the break we'll be moving to a different location for a video presentation,

51
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:33,900
so instead of coming back here

52
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:38,000
we'd like you all to go to Lecture Room three-one-one.

53
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,510
You'll find it on this same level, just down the hall,

54
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:50,300
and there you will be shown a video about important safety issues in the workplace, called Safety at Work.

55
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:52,553
We'll finish off the morning with lunch,

56
00:03:52,553 --> 00:03:57,059
which should give everyone a chance to meet and get to know each other,

57
00:03:57,059 --> 00:04:00,720
and we'll be serving you a buffet lunch in the Main Hall

58
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:04,140
which is on the first floor, from 12.00 o'clock.

59
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:08,468
After lunch you'll be divided up into your teams to meet your team leaders

60
00:04:08,468 --> 00:04:15,270
and we're hoping to be all finished by 3.00 so I won't delay you any longer, and I'll hand over to...
